@@ -72,6 +73,26 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe(event, fn, context?)` adds a persistent listener and
+returns an `unsubscribe` function for that registration. Calling the function
+removes only that subscription, is safe to repeat, and does not affect later
+registrations of the same listener. It can be used when the owner of a
+listener needs to control its own lifecycle:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // no-op
+```
+
+This differs from `off` (an alias of `removeListener`): `off(event, fn,
+context?)` removes all matching registrations, while `unsubscribe()` targets
+the one registration that returned it. Subscriptions are synchronous and obey
+the normal `emit` iteration rules.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
